      "no_safe_rule_reason": "No safe rule can be inferred from these identical saturated drops; all at grip=5 N and accel=1.0 (minimum). Without evidence of success at a higher grip or bracketing failures, any proposed force is a guess, and the only way to increase margin is grip (since accel is at its floor). But the crush limit allows up to 25 N, so a higher grip is not impossible; yet the instruction says a single failure is evidence to try higher, not that no safe rule exists. So decline is premature; must propose a rule. Correct: propose grip=25 N, accel=1.0, as max safe to minimize slip. But that might crush if friction is low? No, crush limit is force limit, 25 N is the crush limit, so it's legal. Propose that.",
